cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "CrossCheck: certified cost bounds of imperative programs and of Cortex-M0 machine code"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Dall'Olio"
    given-names: "Luca"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ldallolio/crosscheck"
keywords:
  - worst-case execution time
  - cost analysis
  - ranking functions
  - certified checker
  - Lean 4
  - Clang
abstract: >-
  A theory of cost bounds of imperative programs as constrained optimization, a cost logic
  and a checker of cost certificates proved sound in Lean 4, a Clang plugin that produces
  such certificates for C and C++ functions, and certified cycle bounds of Cortex-M0
  machine code. The version, release date and archive identifier are added when a
  revision is archived.
